module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FlatFppfInclusion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BaseSites
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ChangeOfSites.ChosenCoarserRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.LocallySurjectiveVanishing
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# A covering family of a flat object consists of flat objects

Let `𝒳` be an algebraic stack over a scheme `S` in a big fppf site `B`, and let `τ` be one of the
five topologies of **Stacks 06TP**. This file proves that the flat objects of `𝒳`
(**Stacks 0787**) are *covering-refinable* for the `τ`-site of `𝒳` in the sense of
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.IsCoveringRefinable`: every `τ`-covering sieve of a flat object contains
a covering family all of whose sources are flat objects.

This is the combinatorial half of clause (2)(a) of **Stacks 0774**, where the source says that
"if `{x_i → x}` is a `τ`-covering of `𝒳`, then each of the morphisms `x_i → x` lies over a flat
morphism of schemes, hence if `x` lies over a scheme `U` such that `x : U → 𝒳` is flat, so do all
of the objects `x_i`". Note that this is genuinely a statement about covering families and not
about all morphisms: an arbitrary morphism into a flat object has no reason to have a flat source,
since an arbitrary morphism of schemes is not flat. That is why the refinement is needed at all,
and it is why `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.IsCoveringRefinable` asks for a presieve inside the given
sieve rather than for a subsieve.

The chain of refinements is the one already used for the fppf topology in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/FlatFppfInclusion.lean`, carried out uniformly in the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind` parameter: a covering sieve of the base topology contains a chosen
covering family of the corresponding kind, hence so does a covering sieve of its localization at
`S`, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology` lifts that
to the site of `𝒳`. A chosen covering family of any of the five kinds is in particular a chosen
*fppf* covering family, so each of its members is flat
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_mem_precoverage`), and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.flatObject_of_flat` turns that into flatness of the sources.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.baseCovering`: the chosen covering families of the indicated one
  of the five big sites carried by a big fppf site, as a single family indexed by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseTopology`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology`: the refinement at
  the three levels — the big site, its localization at `S`, and the site of `𝒳`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCoveringRefinable_flatObject`: the flat objects are
  covering-refinable for each of the five sites of `𝒳`.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.baseCovering` is introduced so that the three refinement
statements can be made once rather than five times. It is defined by the same case distinction
over `AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind` as `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.baseTopology`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.baseTopology_eq_chosenPrecoverage` records that `baseTopology` is
generated by it, which is `rfl` in each of the five cases — including the fppf one, where
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.precoverage_eq_chosenPrecoverage` already identifies the fppf
precoverage with the chosen-family presentation.

That every morphism of the lifted family is strongly cartesian, which is what membership in the
inherited precoverage of **Stacks 06NU** asks for beyond the image being a covering, is free: in a
category fibred in groupoids every morphism is strongly cartesian over its own image
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsFiberedInGroupoids.isStronglyCartesian`). So the family produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology`, which records only
that its image is a chosen covering family, already generates a covering sieve of the site of `𝒳`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03FF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03FF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06NU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06NU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06TP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06TP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0774](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0774)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0787](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0787)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

universe u w v v'

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace BigFppfSite

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u})

/-- The chosen covering families of the indicated one of the five big sites carried by a big fppf
site: the four sub-collections of **Stacks 03FF** and, for `τ = fppf`, the chosen families
themselves. This is the family of covering collections that
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.baseTopology` is generated by. -/
def baseCovering : SiteKind → Covering B.Schemes → Prop
  | .zariski => B.zariskiCovering
  | .etale => B.etaleCovering
  | .smooth => B.smoothCovering
  | .syntomic => B.syntomicCovering
  | .fppf => B.IsCovering

/-- A chosen covering family of any of the five kinds is a chosen fppf covering family. -/
theorem isCovering_of_baseCovering {τ : SiteKind} {E : Covering B.Schemes}
    (hE : B.baseCovering τ E) : B.IsCovering E := by
  cases τ with
  | fppf => exact hE
  | zariski => exact hE.1
  | etale => exact hE.1
  | smooth => exact hE.1
  | syntomic => exact hE.1

/-- Each of the five base topologies is the one generated by the chosen covering families of its
own kind. -/
theorem baseTopology_eq_chosenPrecoverage (τ : SiteKind) :
    B.baseTopology τ = (B.chosenPrecoverage (B.baseCovering τ)).toGrothendieck := by
  cases τ <;> rfl

/-- A presieve presented by a chosen covering family generates a covering sieve of the base
topology of that family's kind. -/
theorem generate_mem_baseTopology_of_baseCovering (τ : SiteKind) {X : B.Schemes}
    {R : Presieve X} (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X) (hR : R = E.presieve₀)
    (hE : B.baseCovering τ ⟨X, E⟩) : Sieve.generate R ∈ B.baseTopology τ X := by
  rw [baseTopology_eq_chosenPrecoverage]
  exact Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck ⟨E, hR, hE⟩

/-- **A covering sieve of any of the five base topologies contains a chosen covering family of
that kind.** The four coarser cases are
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.exists_zariskiCovering_le_of_mem_zariskiTopology` and its
companions, and the fppf case is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_covering_le_of_mem_topology`. -/
theorem exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseTopology (τ : SiteKind) {X : B.Schemes} {R : Sieve X}
    (hR : R ∈ B.baseTopology τ X) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X, B.baseCovering τ ⟨X, E⟩ ∧ E.presieve₀ ≤ R.arrows := by
  cases τ with
  | fppf => exact exists_covering_le_of_mem_topology B hR
  | zariski => exact B.exists_zariskiCovering_le_of_mem_zariskiTopology hR
  | etale => exact B.exists_etaleCovering_le_of_mem_etaleTopology hR
  | smooth => exact B.exists_smoothCovering_le_of_mem_smoothTopology hR
  | syntomic => exact B.exists_syntomicCovering_le_of_mem_syntomicTopology hR

end BigFppfSite

namespace BigFppfOver

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **A covering sieve of the localization at `S` of any of the five base topologies contains a
chosen covering family of that kind.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseTopology` after localization: a
covering sieve of `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseOverTopology` is by definition one whose
image under `CategoryTheory.Sieve.overEquiv` covers downstairs, and a chosen covering family
refining that image is read back upstairs by equipping each of its members with the composite
structure morphism to `S`. -/
theorem exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology (τ : SiteKind)
    {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {R : Sieve U} (hR : R ∈ baseOverTopology B S hS τ U) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} U,
      B.baseCovering τ ⟨(forget B S hS).obj U, E.map (forget B S hS)⟩ ∧
        E.presieve₀ ≤ R.arrows := by
  rw [baseOverTopology, GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff] at hR
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hle⟩ := B.exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseTopology τ hR
  refine ⟨⟨E.I₀, fun i => Over.mk (E.f i ≫ U.hom), fun i => Over.homMk (E.f i) rfl⟩, ?_, ?_⟩
  · change B.baseCovering τ ⟨U.left, _⟩
    simpa [PreZeroHypercover.map] using hE
  · rw [Presieve.ofArrows_le_iff]
    intro i
    exact (Sieve.overEquiv_iff R (E.f i)).mp (hle _ _ ⟨i⟩)

end BigFppfOver

namespace Stack

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **A covering sieve of any of the five sites of a category fibred in groupoids contains a
family whose image is a chosen covering family of that kind.** The
`AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind`-indexed instance of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology`, its base-level input
being `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology`. -/
theorem exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology {X : Type v} [Category.{v'} X]
    (p : X ⥤ BigFppfOver B S hS) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (τ : SiteKind)
    ⦃y : X⦄ (T : Sieve y) (hT : T ∈ BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ y) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} y,
      B.baseCovering τ ⟨(BigFppfOver.forget B S hS).obj (p.obj y),
        (E.map p).map (BigFppfOver.forget B S hS)⟩ ∧ E.presieve₀ ≤ T.arrows :=
  exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology B S hS p (B.baseTopology τ)
    (fun E => B.baseCovering τ ⟨(BigFppfOver.forget B S hS).obj E.1,
      E.2.map (BigFppfOver.forget B S hS)⟩)
    (fun _ _ hR =>
      BigFppfOver.exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology B S hS τ hR) hp T hT

variable (𝒳 : Stack.AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS)

/-- **Stacks 0774**, the step *"if `{x_i → x}` is a `τ`-covering then each `x_i → x` lies over a
flat morphism of schemes, so `x` flat forces every `x_i` flat"* of the proof of clause (2)(a):
the flat objects of an algebraic stack are covering-refinable for each of the five sites of
**Stacks 06TP**.

Every covering sieve of a flat object therefore contains a covering family of flat objects, which
is what makes vanishing of sections at the flat objects — the parasitic condition of
**Stacks 0773** — stable under sheafification. -/
theorem isCoveringRefinable_flatObject (τ : SiteKind) :
    Presheaf.IsCoveringRefinable
      (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p τ) (flatObject B S hS 𝒳.val) := by
  intro y hy T hT
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hle⟩ := exists_baseCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology B S hS
    𝒳.val.val.p 𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids τ T hT
  have hmem : ((E.map 𝒳.val.val.p).map (BigFppfOver.forget B S hS)).presieve₀ ∈
      B.precoverage ((BigFppfOver.forget B S hS).obj (𝒳.val.val.p.obj y)) :=
    ⟨_, rfl, B.isCovering_of_baseCovering hE⟩
  refine ⟨E.presieve₀, hle, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [BigFppfOver.associatedTopology, Functor.inheritedTopology_eq]
    apply Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck
    refine ⟨fun _ f _ => 𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids.isStronglyCartesian f, ?_⟩
    rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff, BigFppfOver.baseOverTopology,
      GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff, Sieve.overEquiv_generate,
      ← Sieve.arrows_generate_map_eq_functorPushforward, Sieve.generate_sieve]
    exact B.generate_mem_baseTopology_of_baseCovering τ
      ((E.map 𝒳.val.val.p).map (BigFppfOver.forget B S hS))
      (by simp only [PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map]) hE
  · rintro z f ⟨i⟩
    exact flatObject_of_flat B S hS 𝒳 (E.f i)
      (flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_mem_precoverage B _ hmem _
        (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i)).1 hy

end Stack

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
